  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Ricochet shots (bouncing off walls) deal full contact damage to all enemies in the path—aim for wall bounces that pass through multiple enemies rather than direct shots at a single target.",
      "Bump Combos activate when monsters in your party are adjacent to each other at the end of a turn—plan launches to cluster your monsters together post-bounce to trigger multiple Bump Combos simultaneously.",
      "Barrier and elemental weakness interactions multiply damage: hitting an enemy's elemental weakness while breaking their barrier in the same hit deals 3× multiplied damage versus hitting the weakness alone.",
      "Mega Luck (LUCK up to 200) increases the chance of monster drops from Quests—farming LUCK by repeatedly clearing specific dungeons with a LUCK-boosting monster in your party maximises rare monster drop rates.",
      "Cross battle (4-player multiplayer) requires coordination: communicate which boss area you are targeting before your turn using the reaction system to avoid all four players attacking the same zone when different zones need coverage."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "リコシェットショット（壁から跳ね返り）は経路上の全ての敵に全接触ダメージを与える。単一ターゲットへの直接ショットより、複数の敵を通過する壁バウンドを狙う。",
      "バンプコンボはターン終了時にパーティのモンスターが互いに隣接している時に発動する。バウンス後にモンスターをクラスター化して複数のバンプコンボを同時にトリガーするためにランチを計画する。",
      "バリアと属性弱点の相互作用はダメージを乗算する。同じヒットでバリアを破壊しながら敵の属性弱点を突くと、弱点を突くだけの3倍のダメージが与えられる。",
      "メガラック（LUCK最大200）はクエストからのモンスタードロップ確率を増加させる。LUCKブーストモンスターをパーティに入れて特定のダンジョンを繰り返しクリアしてLUCKをファームし、希少モンスタードロップ率を最大化する。",
      "クロスバトル（4人マルチプレイヤー）は協調が必要。リアクションシステムを使用して自分のターン前に狙っているボスエリアを伝える。異なるゾーンのカバーが必要な時に全4人が同じゾーンを攻撃するのを避ける。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Core Shot Mechanics",
        "body": "Monster Strike's core mechanic is the slingshot launch: drag back to set trajectory, release to launch. The critical skill is predicting where ricocheted shots travel after wall contacts—spend the first 20 hours exclusively in lower-difficulty dungeons practising 2-wall ricochet paths before attempting boss dungeons. Direct hits deal 100% damage; wall-bounce hits deal 80% but the ability to hit 3–4 enemies simultaneously in a single bounce makes wall shots significantly higher total damage in most encounters."
      },
      {
        "title": "Team Composition Basics",
        "body": "Build teams with at least 2 of the same Bump Combo type (Homing, Spread, etc.) to trigger consecutive Bump Combos that deal stacking damage. Use elemental advantage against the dungeon's primary enemy element—a 4-Attribute-advantage team deals 1.6× the damage of a neutral-element team. Include one monster with an Anti-Gravity barrier ability for dungeons with barrier-protected bosses; without barrier-breaking tools, some bosses take 50% reduced damage for all hits."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Dungeon Modifier Management",
        "body": "Higher-difficulty dungeons add modifier panels (Mines, Damage Walls, Anti-Magic panels) that change the safe launch trajectory. Damage Walls deal percentage-based damage per contact—reduce wall-bouncing in dungeons with Damage Walls and prioritise direct paths. Anti-Magic panels disable Bump Combo effects—steer monsters away from Anti-Magic panels on turns where Bump Combos are critical to the clear pattern. Study the dungeon layout at the start of each floor to identify panel positions before your first launch."
      },
      {
        "title": "Lucky Creature and Event Farming",
        "body": "Lucky Creatures appear in selected dungeons and grant LUCK bonuses and orbs when hit—maximise Lucky Creature contacts by bouncing shots to pass through the Creature multiple times rather than hitting it once. During event periods, Lucky Creature bonuses stack with event multipliers; farming Lucky Creature-enabled event dungeons during active events provides the highest combined LUCK and material income per stamina spent."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Ultimate Quest Strategies",
        "body": "Ultimate Quests (high-difficulty permanent content) require specific counter-builds assembled from rare monsters with boss-counter abilities. The most important Ultimate Quest preparation: identify the 3 primary mechanics of the boss (barrier type, elemental weakness, phase-change trigger) from the community database before farming materials. Attempting Ultimate Quests without the correct counter-build wastes time and stamina regardless of team level."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Launching without predicting bounce paths—uninstructed launches that hit walls randomly deal less total damage than a planned 1-bounce path to a weak point; always visualise the full shot trajectory before releasing.",
      "Ignoring monster type interactions (Speed vs. Power vs. Technique vs. Balance)—type advantage provides 10% attack bonus; maintaining 2+ type-matched monsters in your party guarantees consistent passive advantage.",
      "Not using friend monsters—the Friend Monster slot provides access to monsters outside your roster; using a friend's maxed-out premium monster is equivalent to adding a fully invested party member for free.",
      "Spending orbs on non-premium gachas—basic orb draws provide common monsters; premium draws (4-orb) provide significantly higher chance for rare limited monsters and should be saved for limited event draws.",
      "Fighting multiplayer bosses without mobile device health—Monster Strike multiplayer sessions last 10–15 minutes; running out of battery mid-session forces a disconnect penalty that costs the entire clear reward."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "バウンスパスを予測せずにランチする。壁にランダムに当たる無計画なランチは、弱点への計画された1バウンスパスより合計ダメージが少ない。解放前に常に全ショット軌道を視覚化する。",
      "モンスタータイプの相互作用を無視する（スピード vs. パワー vs. テクニック vs. バランス）。タイプ有利は10%の攻撃ボーナスを提供する。パーティに2体以上のタイプマッチモンスターを維持すると一貫したパッシブ有利が保証される。",
      "フレンドモンスターを使わない。フレンドモンスタースロットはロースター外のモンスターへのアクセスを提供する。フレンドの最大プレミアムモンスターを使うことは、無料で完全投資されたパーティメンバーを追加するのと同等。",
      "非プレミアムガチャにオーブを使う。基本オーブ引きは一般的なモンスターを提供する。プレミアム引き（4オーブ）は希少な限定モンスターの確率がかなり高く、限定イベント引きのために貯めるべき。",
      "モバイルデバイスのバッテリーなしでマルチプレイヤーボスと戦う。モンスターストライクのマルチプレイヤーセッションは10〜15分続く。セッション途中のバッテリー切れは全クリア報酬を失う接続切断ペナルティを引き起こす。"
    ]
